    "digdeeper": {
      "type": "zeta-accordion",
      "blocks": {
        "a1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Description",
            "content": "<h3>Patented High-Leucine EAAs + L-Arginine for <em>muscle &amp; longevity</em>.</h3><p>ZETA MINOS delivers a unique, patented essential amino acid blend in a single 7g scoop — featuring all <strong>9 EAAs</strong> with a powerful <strong>1.5g of L-Leucine</strong> plus a deliberate addition of <strong>L-Arginine (405 mg)</strong>. This complete profile is specifically designed to trigger muscle protein synthesis (MPS), fight sarcopenia, and support lifelong strength and vitality.</p><h4>Why we added L-Arginine — the smart advantage</h4><p>Most EAA formulas stop at the basics. ZETA MINOS goes further by including L-Arginine, a strategic choice backed by science:</p><ul>\n<li>Acts as a <strong>precursor to nitric oxide</strong> — improving blood flow, oxygen, and nutrient delivery to working muscles</li>\n<li>Supports better muscle perfusion and recovery — especially important as we age</li>\n<li>Studies on EAA + Arginine supplementation in older adults showed meaningful gains in lean body mass, strength, and physical function — benefits beyond EAAs alone</li>\n</ul><p style=\"font-size:11.5px;color:var(--zeta-mid);font-style:italic;margin-top:28px;\">*These statements have not been evaluated by the Food and Drug Administration. This product is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease.</p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          }
        },
        "a2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Ingredients",
            "content": "<h3>What's <em>in it.</em></h3><h4>Supplement Facts</h4><p><strong>Serving size:</strong> 1 scoop (~7 g) · <strong>Servings per canister:</strong> 30 · <strong>Net wt:</strong> 7.41 oz (210 g)</p><p><strong>Patented High-Leucine EAA + L-Arginine Blend</strong> (research-backed ratios):</p><ul>\n<li>\n<strong>L-Leucine — 1,500 mg</strong> (the mTOR trigger; dosed to clear the age-elevated threshold)</li>\n<li>L-Lysine HCl — 672 mg</li>\n<li>L-Valine — 427 mg</li>\n<li>L-Isoleucine — 414 mg</li>\n<li>\n<strong>L-Arginine — 405 mg</strong> (the smart advantage; nitric oxide precursor)</li>\n<li>L-Threonine — 363 mg</li>\n<li>L-Phenylalanine — 260 mg</li>\n<li>L-Methionine — 128 mg</li>\n<li>L-Histidine — 64 mg</li>\n<li>L-Tryptophan — 2.5 mg</li>\n</ul><h4>Other Ingredients</h4><p>Natural fruit punch flavor. Sweetened with monk fruit/stevia. No artificial sweeteners, sugar alcohols, or synthetic flavors.</p><h4>Why this ratio</h4><p>Most \"BCAA\" powders use a 2:1:1 ratio and stop there. MINOS delivers all 9 EAAs with leucine at the high end (1.5g — enough to fire mTOR in aging bodies) plus L-Arginine for the nitric oxide pathway. Full anabolic stack, in one scoop.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "a3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Directions & Precautions",
            "content": "<h3>How to <em>take it.</em></h3><p><strong>Mix 1 scoop into 8–12 oz of cold water.</strong> Drink any time of day — amino acids are precursors to protein, so your body uses them whenever you take them. Don't exceed 2 scoops in a day.</p><h4>Best Times</h4><ul>\n<li>\n<strong>Morning</strong> — with breakfast, for an early MPS pulse</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Pre-workout</strong> — primes the muscle to use amino acids during training</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Intra-workout</strong> — sip during long sessions for sustained delivery</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Post-workout</strong> — the classic recovery window</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Between meals</strong> — bridges the gap on lower-protein eating days</li>\n</ul><h4>Pairs Well With</h4><ul>\n<li>\n<strong>Z-83</strong> — focus + clean energy before the workout</li>\n<li>\n<strong>ZETA CREATINE</strong> — strength + power output</li>\n<li>\n<strong>ZETA MULTI</strong> — daily vitamin foundation</li>\n</ul><h4>Precautions</h4><p>If pregnant, nursing, or under 18, consult your healthcare provider. If you have kidney conditions or are on a protein-restricted diet, check with your physician. Not a meal replacement.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "a4": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Research",
            "content": "<h3>The <em>research</em> underneath.</h3><p>Two pieces of the MINOS science deserve highlighting: <strong>(1)</strong> why we added L-Arginine (Børsheim 2008) and <strong>(2)</strong> why we dose leucine high in older adults (Katsanos 2006). Plus the broader literature behind EAA supplementation for muscle and longevity.</p><div class=\"acc-highlight\"><div class=\"hl-label\">★ Key study · the EAA + Arginine paper</div><p><strong>Børsheim E, Bui Q-UT, Tissier S, Kobayashi H, Ferrando AA, Wolfe RR (2008).</strong> <em>Effect of amino acid supplementation on muscle mass, strength and physical function in elderly.</em> <strong>Clinical Nutrition.</strong></p><p>16-week double-blind RCT in glucose-intolerant elderly. EAA + Arginine supplementation between meals significantly increased lean body mass (+1.14 kg at 12 weeks), lower-extremity strength (+22%), and physical function including gait speed and mobility.</p></div><h4>Supporting research</h4><div class=\"ref\"><strong>Noh KW, et al. (2025).</strong> <em>Effects of amino acid supplementation on muscle protein metabolism and adaptation: a narrative review.</em> <strong>Physical Activity and Nutrition.</strong></div><div class=\"ref\"><strong>Church DD, Ferrando AA, Wolfe RR (2024).</strong> <em>Stimulation of muscle protein synthesis with low-dose amino acid composition in older individuals.</em> <strong>Frontiers in Nutrition.</strong></div><div class=\"ref\"><strong>Katsanos CS, et al. (2006).</strong> <em>A high proportion of leucine is required for optimal stimulation of the rate of muscle protein synthesis by essential amino acids in the elderly.</em> <strong>American Journal of Physiology.</strong> <em>→ The science behind our 1.5 g L-Leucine dose.</em></div>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [ "a1", "a2", "a3", "a4" ],
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "For the Curious",
        "heading": "Dig <em>deeper.</em>",
